{# How to read e-mail documents. The message fields come from `doc_email`, the text from
   `read_documents`. Each sentence that names a tool renders only when the run has it. #}
Reading e-mail documents

{% if has('search_collections') %}
Find e-mails with {{ tool('search_collections') }}. Put every form of an address or a name into one call, for example the address, "First Last" and "Last, First".

{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_email') %}
1. Call {{ tool('doc_email') }} with the file_hash of the e-mail. It gives the sender, the recipients, the copies, the date, the subject, the parent message, the attachments and the message graph.
2. To follow a thread, give node, the file hash of another message in the graph. The graph then centres on that message.
3. An attachment is a document of its own. Read it with its own file_hash.
{% endif %}
{% if has('read_documents') %}
4. Read the text of the message with {{ tool('read_documents') }}.
{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_metadata') %}
5. For the headers and the dates that are not in the text, call {{ tool('doc_metadata') }}.
{% endif %}

A copy of the same message can be in more than one mailbox. Compare its fields when a count depends on distinct messages.

{% if has('doc_email') %}
{{ tool('doc_email') }} requires collection and file_hash.
collection is one name. file_hash accepts one hash or a list of up to ten hashes from that collection.
node optionally centres the graph on a returned message hash. Omission centres it on the requested email.
Use more with read_more to inspect remaining attachments and graph entries.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH"}
```
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":["COPY_EMAIL_HASH_1","COPY_EMAIL_HASH_2"],"node":"COPY_GRAPH_MESSAGE_HASH"}
```
{% endif %}
{% if has('doc_metadata') %}
{{ tool('doc_metadata') }} requires collection and file_hash. It accepts one hash or a list of up to ten hashes.
It returns stored metadata, dates, locations and download links. Use read_more for remaining metadata fields.
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":"COPY_RETURNED_HASH"}
```
```json
{"collection":"alpha","file_hash":["COPY_EMAIL_HASH_1","COPY_EMAIL_HASH_2"]}
```
{% endif %}
Read the requested passage before assigning its writer, recipients or date.
The outer email envelope belongs to the outer message.
A forwarded or quoted passage can have a different writer, recipients and date.
Use that passage's own headers to identify who wrote it.
A person who forwarded a message did not necessarily write its quoted statement.
When attribution remains unknown, state that limit.
Read passages for targeted ranges and continuation instructions. Do not repeat the initial read to request later text.
